    "faq": {
      "tag": "FAQ",
      "title": "Answers to Your Frequently Asked Questions",
      "q1": "When was Bukhara State Technical University (BSTU) established?",
      "a1": "BSTU was officially established in January 2025 by Presidential Resolution No. PP-22, uniting the Bukhara Engineering-Technological Institute and the Bukhara Institute of Natural Resources Management.",
      "q2": "What main faculties are available at BSTU?",
      "a2": "The university is structured into 4 faculties and 24 departments, including Chemical & Food Technologies, Oil & Gas Technology, Engineering & Construction, Power Engineering & ICT, Textile & Light Industry, and Natural Resources Management.",
      "q3": "Does BSTU offer joint or double-degree educational programs?",
      "a3": "Yes, BSTU active partnerships offer double-degree and joint educational programs with leading technical universities in Latvia, Malaysia, Belarus, and Russia.",
      "q4": "What is the Advanced Engineering School at BSTU?",
      "a4": "Established in cooperation with Uzbekneftegaz JSC, the Advanced Engineering School aims to provide energy sector students with hands-on, high-tech industrial training and direct career pathways.",
      "q5": "Where is the main university campus located?",
      "a5": "The university campus is located at 15 Q. Murtazoyev Street, Bukhara city, Uzbekistan.",
      "q6": "Who is the Rector of Bukhara State Technical University?",
      "a6": "The university is led by Rector Sadoqat Ghaforovna Siddikova, appointed to guide the institution through its technological and academic advancements."
    },
